type: software
title: "The maximum Wiener index of trees with prescribed diameter: the sharp second-order constant"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. Among trees with n vertices and diameter d, the largest Wiener index (sum of all pairwise distances) lies just below (d/2 - eps/4)n^2, eps the parity of d. Cambie (2020) showed that the shortfall has order (dn)^(3/2) and placed its coefficient between sqrt(2)/3 and 29/60 in iterated limits. Whenever d tends to infinity and d/n tends to 0 the shortfall is (kappa + o(1))(dn)^(3/2) with kappa = sqrt((175 - sqrt 7)/756), about 0.47747. For each fixed d >= 4 the coefficients of n^(3/2) and n are rational constants computed from the effective resistance of small rooted trees; for large n every maximiser is built from a finite catalogue of branch shapes, so an exact algorithm polynomial in log n exists; and the maximum and all maximisers are given explicitly for diameter five and every n >= 6."
